# Production transport, baked into the bundle at build time.
#
# Vite substitutes import.meta.env.* during `vite build`, so these cannot be
# changed after the fact by editing a hosting dashboard -- a variable added
# there only takes effect on the NEXT build. Committing them here means a push
# is enough to produce a correctly wired bundle.
#
# The host is the Vercel project built from this repository's root directory,
# whose entrypoint is api/index.py. It must be named `rakshyanet-api` for this
# hostname to resolve; if Vercel appends a suffix because the name was taken,
# change the line below and push again.
#
# There is deliberately no VITE_WS_URL. Vercel serverless functions cannot hold
# a connection open, so no WebSocket endpoint exists in this deployment at all.
# Pointing the client at one would only produce a doomed connection and a
# console full of errors; useWebSocket treats an absent URL as "no realtime
# transport here" and says so in the UI rather than retrying forever.
#
# No secrets belong in this file. Vite exposes every VITE_-prefixed variable to
# the browser, so anything written here is public. API keys stay on the backend.
VITE_API_URL=https://rakshyanet-api.vercel.app
